course: dictionary
lesson: 9792
title: One word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word suspect can be a verb, a noun or an adjective, so its meaning depends on its job in the sentence. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. Ask: is someone doing something, is it a person, or is it a description?
explain: As a verb, suspect means to think something is probably true without being sure. «I suspect it will rain» means you believe rain is likely, but you have no proof yet. It can also mean to think someone may have done something wrong: «suspect him of lying» means you think he is lying.
explain: As a noun, a suspect is a person the police think may have done a crime. «The police catch and question suspects» means the people they are checking. A suspect is not proven guilty; they are a person of interest, not yet a criminal. As an adjective, suspect means possibly false, dangerous or not to be trusted, as in «a suspect package».
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «I suspect so» means I think that is probably true. If your meaning still makes sense in the sentence, you have probably got it right.
fact: Suspect can be a verb, a noun or an adjective.
fact: As a verb, «suspect» means to think something is probably true, or to think someone may have done something wrong.
fact: A «suspect» is a person the police think may have done a crime. The usual suspect is a guess, not proof.
fact: As an adjective, «suspect» means possibly false, dangerous or not to be trusted, as in «a suspect package».
fact: In safety, report a suspect package or a suspected scam to an adult.
exercise: «I suspect it will rain.» What does suspect mean here? | *To think something is probably true, without being sure | To be certain something is true | To hide something from people | To catch a criminal
exercise: «The police catch and question suspects.» In this sentence, what is a suspect? | A court where the law is decided | A police car | *A person the police think may have done a crime | A rule everyone must follow
exercise: «Do not touch that suspect package; tell an adult.» What does suspect mean in «a suspect package»? | *Possibly dangerous or not to be trusted | Brightly coloured | Sent by post, and always safe | Very heavy
test: Ravi says, «I suspect him of lying.» What does suspect mean? | *To think he may have done something wrong | To tell him a joke | To be sure he is telling the truth | To forget what he said
test: «She reported a suspected scam to the bank.» What does suspected mean? | *Possibly a trick, and not to be trusted | A happy surprise | Something very old | A kind of sweet
exam: In «The main suspect was seen near the bank», what kind of word is suspect? | A number | An adjective | A verb | *A noun
